# Pinned sources for `snapintosh build`. Override any value in the environment or in
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/snapintosh/pins.env.
#
# Nothing of ours is public yet, so QEMU_REPO, REIMS_REPO and M2V_REPO default to empty and `build` refuses to
# guess. For local testing point them at file:// remotes of your own clones.

# QEMU fork: lab branch p89b, commit 18bbe3b54b "fix(vmapple):
# count the sync-clock-on-load advance from the stop". This is what the lab binary qemu-p8p89q (md5 4381561b...)
# was built from, plus the G5 relink below. p89b = d3 (876cba5472: p79 IOFence patch, any-build matcher, vmapple
# ambrosia=on, PAuth key copy, avp-rtc VMState, P82/P84b early pack open, P84 slirp ARP seed, P86 DSB skips)
# plus 4 commits, kept as patches/qemu/0001..0004 (git format-patch 876cba5472..18bbe3b54b): P89 (the pack ages itself),
# P89b (compaction moved off the exit path into the qemu-pcache-compact tool, hash precheck in the lookup),
# the compactor's age table, and the Q3 sync-clock fix. `make install` installs qemu-pcache-compact next to qemu.
# The branch q2 (guest clock dilation for slow hosts) is NOT the default.
# Nothing is public yet.
# R12: the same tree as p89b 18bbe3b54b regrouped into 20 commits on upstream v11.1.0 (84f07211cc), branch
# release-v0 of the laptop clone qemu-r6b, head 297e317b64 (`git diff 18bbe3b54b 297e317b64` is empty). Same tree means the same
# bytes: the build gives md5 9c12eb7b... either way. The pin changes only because the commit id does. Up to R11 the pin was
# 18bbe3b54b8a7863cc6378f8d64db94b9fa1716e; a bare repo that serves only that commit needs the new one fetched (or QEMU_REF set back).
# Nothing is pushed: the repo that serves 297e317b64 has to be made from release-v0.
# R13: release-v0 was rebased once, fixing -Werror=missing-prototypes for p35_arm_tlbi in commit 9 (prototype in
# target/arm/internals.h). Head e475148e2f569c6d3562021b12990e8f94a19cef (old head 297e317b64, branch release-v0-r12); the tree differs from p89b only by
# that prototype move. `build` now passes a fixed configure feature set, so the reference md5 is independent of installed packages:
# qemu-system-aarch64 cf135e84fec1907c762beb52925fa288 on Debian 13 (minimal, with ~190 dev packages and on the full lab host), 7a27d6f4a0181de261f5938440365958 on Ubuntu 26.04 (other gcc).
# The old reference 9c12eb7b... (every optional feature on) is gone, so the translation cache pack is new.
QEMU_REPO=${QEMU_REPO:-}
# R16: P97 added on top of release-v0 as branch release-v1, head b8b80ad5439ac06c1e4a0704e3e5dc7cd32e1664
# (two commits, accel/tcg/pcache.c only: the exit no longer msyncs the pack, qemu-pcache-compact fdatasyncs it; cherry-picked from the lab branch
# p97, 1a6cbc98a5 and 1de04eefe0). Reference md5 on Debian 13: qemu-system-aarch64 455899b7d68dbf7ff41b8cec5a603956 (libreims_vgpu.a unchanged,
# 97230a90...). The binary is new, so its translation pack is new. release-v0 (e475148e2f, md5 cf135e84...) stays the pin for builds without P97.
# R30: release-v2 = release-v1 plus the P102 BQL spin, branch release-v2, head 8df7ee62c81bc602b0eec0cd23c1fa11994a7094 (two commits on b8b80ad543, both in
# system/cpus.c: a vCPU thread that wants the big QEMU lock spins for 50 us before it sleeps; P102_BQLSPIN=0 turns the spin off, P102_BQLSPIN=N sets
# N microseconds). patches/qemu/0005..0008 are `git format-patch release-v0..release-v2` (the P97 and P102 commits on top of release-v0). Reference md5 on
# Debian 13: qemu-system-aarch64 c36556f3118e04fca90005ae0f0dfd68 (libreims_vgpu.a unchanged, 97230a90a5d39d85f79df52358096de2). The binary is new, so its
# translation pack is new. Ubuntu 26.04 (gcc 15.2): qemu-system-aarch64 7bca48fbfa6f6d4954b5643890243d61, libreims_vgpu.a 3105d01f51d9b335d731c5b0ed1be662 (A4, clean VM).
# release-v1 (b8b80ad543, md5 455899b7...) stays the pin for a build without the spin. SNAPSHOT_STATE_FORMAT below is unchanged:
# the commits touch no vmstate section and no machine layout, a snapshot of release-v1 resumes with release-v2 and the other way round.
QEMU_REF=${QEMU_REF:-8df7ee62c81bc602b0eec0cd23c1fa11994a7094}

# reims-vgpu and metal2vulkan: the exact trees qemu-p8p89q (md5 4381561b...) was linked from (G5 relink, 2026-11-19,
# tools/g5/relink.py method). Lab branch g5-fewer-vk-reqs off p70-backport: metal2vulkan e0a40424 (6 commits on
# d4ac1fd7: unordered framebuffer fetch without an interlock, no-copy buffers over dma-bufs without host-pointer
# import, lab switches M2V_NO_INTERLOCK and M2V_NO_HOSTPTR) and reims-vgpu 4969eab6 (one commit on f54dcb4f, counts
# dma-buf host-memory import). On a GPU that has the extensions the preferred paths still run; the fallbacks only
# apply where they are missing. Dist library libreims_vgpu.a md5 036e46dc... .
# The earlier pair (D3, qemu-p8d3) was reims-vgpu 01117f6c and metal2vulkan d4ac1fd7; both still work with this QEMU
# but lack the fallbacks.
# P93: reims-vgpu 81e0125b, branch p93-suspend-order, one commit on 4969eab6
# (kept as patches/reims/0001): the wake after a save resumes the device in place, which lost the root FIFO and the
# stamp memory, so a child FIFO's next barrier or stamp aborted the save (device.stamp.read_without_memory). Lab
# binary qemu-p8p93 (md5 8b986617...) = qemu-p8p89q relinked against it (dist libreims_vgpu.a md5 3a492a9b...).
# reims-vgpu expects metal2vulkan as a sibling directory (its Cargo.toml patches the git dependency to ../metal2vulkan).
REIMS_REPO=${REIMS_REPO:-}
REIMS_REF=${REIMS_REF:-81e0125b5594639caff4a3fc7e38446e00cb499b}
M2V_REPO=${M2V_REPO:-}
M2V_REF=${M2V_REF:-e0a4042424a36d96822b7eb7ab54f6a3af5ad1e2}

# Snapshot state format. A snapshot resumes with any build that has the same value: the QEMU
# fork's migration stream (vmstate of the vmapple machine and devices, from QEMU_REF) plus the renderer's suspend blob
# (reims-vgpu guest/abi/suspend_blob.rs, magic RVGS version 1). Relinking a renderer fix that leaves both alone (P93) keeps the
# value. BUMP IT whenever QEMU_REF changes a vmstate section or machine layout, or the blob version changes: `build` then keeps
# the old binary for the snapshots that still need it and `resume` picks it. Wrongly unchanged means a resume that fails to load or
# misbehaves; wrongly bumped only costs a kept binary.
SNAPSHOT_STATE_FORMAT=${SNAPSHOT_STATE_FORMAT:-vmapple-18bbe3b54b-rvgs1}

# Ambrosia (boot firmware, replaces Apple's AVPBooter and iBoot). Upstream is public. Tag v0.1.3 plus our 3
# optional-key patches in patches/ambrosia (KeepAppleGfx, Chosen, Asmb; the lab clone r4/ambrosia has them as
# commits, head 2fa868c2daa6). License GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, our patches follow it.
# Builds with rust 1.99.1 (its rust-toolchain.toml) and the aarch64-unknown-none target, one `make`.
AMBROSIA_REPO=${AMBROSIA_REPO:-https://github.com/steelbrain/ambrosia.git}
AMBROSIA_REF=${AMBROSIA_REF:-1b924d95f077b6e84f300f40fe1dbd1788772f69}
AMBROSIA_PATCHED_HEAD=2fa868c2daa62128f78d01728379e31da76c05e5
# Image the lab runs (data/r4/ambrosia-r4.bin). `build` reproduces it byte for byte with rust 1.99.1 and warns if not.
AMBROSIA_SHA256=${AMBROSIA_SHA256:-586f6c7be1622a1f80c52e3fc1ab210464eb2b8e272616334625d940d66f0a73}

# Guest policy keys the lab needs under Ambrosia (findings 1 and 2 of the Ambrosia bring-up): internal-use-only-unit
# lets the Data volume mount, lp-sip0=127 (0x7f) is the old csr-config=0x7f and is needed for speed. Not a
# SIP-on configuration. Written into config.plist, packed as config.cpio, loaded at 0x120000000.
AMBROSIA_BOOTARGS=${AMBROSIA_BOOTARGS:--v}
AMBROSIA_LP_SIP0=${AMBROSIA_LP_SIP0:-127}

# Mesa, only for hosts without a usable Vulkan GPU (lavapipe). Stock lavapipe 25.0.x lacks
# VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock, which the renderer requires. The lab runs Mesa 26.3.0
# development (0a6fa60abb73) plus patches/mesa-lavapipe-immutable-samplers.patch.
MESA_REPO=${MESA_REPO:-https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.git}
MESA_REF=${MESA_REF:-0a6fa60abb737d26ac8a316a4aad7c9ddf64f9e4}

# Tested guest builds. `snapintosh fetch --build B` picks one; Apple's CDN serves the file, we never host it.
# 26A428 (27.0) is the build every lab number comes from and the only one the full stack has booted.
# 26B131 (27.2.1, released 2026-11-09) is the supported second path: the P79
# matcher has its row, Ambrosia upstream lists it as tested, but this stack has NOT booted it, and the quiet
# profile, harness boxes and apple-gfx guest side are unchecked there. Needs its own Mac install and golden.
IPSW_BUILDS="26A428 26B131"
IPSW_DEFAULT=${IPSW_DEFAULT:-26A428}
IPSW_26A428_VERSION=27.0
IPSW_26A428_URL=https://updates.cdn-apple.com/2026FallFCS/afcfc88e-bbe6-44bf-a5da-07c56eebc06c/UniversalMac_27.0_26A428_Restore.ipsw
IPSW_26A428_SHA256=2a5d3c695d501022b7fad9adaffcf2627bcb867d993fb5662dcd41bac99a2836
IPSW_26A428_SIZE=26626436228
IPSW_26B131_VERSION=27.2.1
IPSW_26B131_URL=https://updates.cdn-apple.com/2026FallFCS/c202a724-db7e-4d56-917b-110aa0226507/UniversalMac_27.2.1_26B131_Restore.ipsw
IPSW_26B131_SHA256=233e85a09887579d47d0b195e7db72be7f204261059c6946f719acf6b300814f
IPSW_26B131_SIZE=25595954706
# Index used to look a build up by id when a URL goes stale (third party, links go to Apple).
IPSW_INDEX=https://api.ipsw.me/v4/device/VirtualMac2,1?type=ipsw

# AVPBooter.vmapple2.bin is NOT a required input any more. Only the legacy path (FW=avp) uses it, and it must come
# from your own Mac (Apple file, never redistributed).
